A||N||2||Tina||Some info needed on quarter window swap.||||5||
Z||000000||Tina||04-09-2001||01:30 PM||||1. Will 84 style fit on a 87 coupe?<BR>2. Can I swap the glass from one window to      the other?<BR>  (Provided their both the 84 style)<BR>3. Does anybody have some laying around, <BR>   and willing to sell ?<P>Thanks Tina||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-09-2001||02:10 PM||||Yes the 84 glass ones will fit the 85-88 notchbacks. You need to get the entire panel and the metal clip behind it. (I have glass ones on my 86 SE) To remove the metal clip (or install it) you need to remove the inside sail panel to access the 10mm nut. I have not tried swapping glass withing the panel so I don't know if it's possible.<BR>Bob Steiger at Twin Lakes Fiero has a number of glass sets. Some are plain and some are "SE" types.<BR>his number is 217-379-9140<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||04-09-2001||03:11 PM||||I've examined the glass sail panels for modification purposes, and didn't find any way to pull the glass from the frame, it appears as though the frame is molded around the glass. I guess you could destroy the frame and extract the glass, but then, that probably wouldn't serve any purpose, since I doubt the glass would fit in a later design frame.||||reg||1
